EVERY FILE IN THIS DIRECTORY that is transcribed from a published document is
third-party material, used as a test fixture. This note covers all files in
this directory, not any single one of them. It does NOT extend to the parent
directory or to any sibling directory.

Work:      Apple II Reference Manual (Monitor ROM listing)
Author:    Apple Computer, Inc.
Published: 1979
Source:    https://archive.org/details/Apple_II_Reference_Manual_1979_Apple

AppleII-1979-MonitorListing.txt is a transcription of the instruction column of
the original Monitor ROM listing printed in that manual. It records addresses,
bytes, mnemonics and operands only, and is used to check that Casso's
disassembler agrees with Apple's own listing. It is not compiled into, linked
into, or distributed with any Casso binary.

Tests MUST treat it as read-only. A mismatch between the listing and Casso is a
finding about Casso, never a reason to edit the transcription, unless the
transcription is shown to differ from the printed page.

Scripts/ holds Casso's own debugger scripts and their expected output. They are
MIT licensed with the rest of Casso.
